{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c41d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b60-5dda-7951-9c64-98cc389b396d"},"sequence":105,"recorded_at":1780531400000205,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a"},"call_id":"call_01a07b608b6e7602bb67a1099394a500","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree/.github/workflows/ci.yml`.\n1|name: CI\n2|\n3|on:\n4|  pull_request:\n5|  push:\n6|    branches:\n7|      - main\n8|\n9|permissions:\n10|  contents: read\n11|\n12|# What green means. Every job below proves its selection matched something:\n13|# a grep, glob, file scan, matrix expansion, or test selector that finds\n14|# nothing fails closed instead of passing on an empty result set. No job\n15|# declares an `if:` condition, so no job can skip quietly; gates-verdict\n16|# additionally refuses any skipped, failed, or cancelled dependency.\n17|#\n18|# GOOS=windows work is compile-and-vet only. A green windows-compile-only job\n19|# proves the tree type-checks for Windows; it never implies executed\n20|# behaviour. Coverage is reported as numbers, not enforced as a floor.\n21|jobs:\n22|  contract-preservation:\n23|    name: Contract preservation (v0.5.0 current, v0.4.3 historical)\n24|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n25|    timeout-minutes: 10\n26|    steps:\n27|      - name: Check out repository\n28|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n29|\n30|      - name: Set up Go\n31|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n32|        with:\n33|          go-version-file: go.mod\n34|\n35|      - name: Verify specification-to-code ownership\n36|        run: go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n37|\n38|      - name: Verify generated catalog is current\n39|        run: |\n40|          go generate ./internal/catalog\n41|          git diff --exit-code -- internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go\n42|\n43|      # The release roots are derived from internal/specpin and\n44|      # internal/catalog inside the gate, never retyped here. Each -- PASS\n45|      # guard below must match: a selector that runs nothing fails here\n46|      # instead of passing silently.\n47|      - name: Run pinned contract-version gates\n48|        run: |\n49|          set +e\n50|          go test ./internal/cigate -run 'TestVerifyContractPreservationLive|TestPinnedReleasesAgreeAcrossAuthorities|TestDerivedSetsAreComplete|TestCheckAgreementAdmitsIdenticalSets|TestCheckAgreementRefusals|TestCheckReleaseRootsRefusesDrift' -count=1 -v > cigate-contracts.log 2>&1\n51|          code=$?\n52|          set -e\n53|          cat cigate-contracts.log\n54|          test $code -eq 0\n55|          for gate in TestVerifyContractPreservationLive TestPinnedReleasesAgreeAcrossAuthorities TestDerivedSetsAreComplete TestCheckAgreementAdmitsIdenticalSets TestCheckAgreementRefusals TestCheckReleaseRootsRefusesDrift; do\n56|            grep -q \"^--- PASS: ${gate}\" cigate-contracts.log\n57|          done\n58|\n59|  lint:\n60|    name: Linters (vet, Windows vet, gofmt)\n61|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n62|    timeout-minutes: 10\n63|    steps:\n64|      - name: Check out repository\n65|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n66|\n67|      - name: Set up Go\n68|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n69|        with:\n70|          go-version-file: go.mod\n71|\n72|      - name: Vet\n73|        run: go vet ./...\n74|\n75|      - name: Vet Windows build-tagged sources\n76|        run: GOOS=windows go vet ./...\n77|\n78|      # gofmt lists only offending files, so a clean tree prints nothing.\n79|      # The file count proves the scan was not empty; the log must then be.\n80|      - name: Check formatting\n81|        run: |\n82|          count=$(find internal -name '*.go' | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\n83|          echo \"go files scanned: ${count}\"\n84|          test \"${count}\" -gt 0\n85|          set +e\n86|          gofmt -l internal > gofmt.log 2>&1\n87|          code=$?\n88|          set -e\n89|          cat gofmt.log\n90|          test $code -eq 0\n91|          test ! -s gofmt.log\n92|\n93|  test:\n94|    name: Build and test (no cache)\n95|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n96|    timeout-minutes: 15\n97|    steps:\n98|      - name: Check out repository\n99|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n100|\n101|      - name: Set up Go\n102|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n103|        with:\n104|          go-version-file: go.mod\n105|\n106|      - name: Build\n107|        run: go build ./...\n108|\n109|      # Verbose on purpose: the --- SKIP lines are the suite-wide skip\n110|      # datum. At least one package must report ok: a suite that matched\n111|      # nothing is a failure, not a pass.\n112|      - name: Test\n113|        run: |\n114|          set +e\n115|          go test ./... -v -count=1 > test.log 2>&1\n116|          code=$?\n117|          set -e\n118|          cat test.log\n119|          test $code -eq 0\n120|          test \"$(grep -c '^ok' test.log)\" -gt 0\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
