{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c483","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b60-5dda-7951-9c64-98cc389b396d"},"sequence":156,"recorded_at":1780531400000307,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"f21e9059-3287-4ccb-9e2d-a0bda30b6475"},"task_id":"f21e9059-3287-4ccb-9e2d-a0bda30b6475","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"f21e9059-3287-4ccb-9e2d-a0bda30b6475","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree/internal/cigate/doc.go`.\n1|// Package cigate implements the M0 continuous-conformance CI gates for the\n2|// security-primitives-and-conformance-ci story: historical and current\n3|// contract preservation, fixture-target derivation, and the\n4|// unsupported-capability advertisement check.\n5|//\n6|// It is a gate, not a second authority. Every behavior it constrains is\n7|// decided by an existing owner; this package only re-derives those decisions\n8|// from their owners and refuses drift:\n9|//\n10|//   - pinned contract versions stay in internal/specpin; the typed release\n11|//     projections stay in internal/catalog. VerifyContractPreservation\n12|//     requires the two authorities to agree exactly and fails closed on a\n13|//     version either side cannot account for;\n14|//   - platform capability availability stays in internal/secconftest probes.\n15|//     CheckAdvertisements takes probe outcomes as input and never defines a\n16|//     capability of its own. CI scans with every probe forced unavailable,\n17|//     which is stronger than live scanning and host-independent; live probe\n18|//     outcomes are read by no call site;\n19|//   - the secconftest fuzz targets stay mapped in FuzzTargetEntry.\n20|//     FuzzTargets derives the committed target list from that map rather\n21|//     than retyping it, and TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation holds CI's\n22|//     `go test -list` leg equal to it. Fuzz targets also live in\n23|//     internal/canonicaljson and internal/scalar, which own no entry map;\n24|//     CI smokes those packages from their own `-list` derivations.\n25|//\n26|// Normative scope: AX v0.5.0 Sections 16, 19.2-19.5, 20.2, Appendix D. The\n27|// Section 19.3 provider suites and Section 19.4 lifecycle cases outside\n28|// Section 16 are not driven here; CI runs them only where their owning\n29|// packages already implement them, and this gate claims nothing about the\n30|// rest.\n31|//\n32|// Stated bounds. The gates are read-only: they parse the pinned authorities\n33|// and repository text and write only their verdict to the caller. They mutate\n34|// no durable state, keep no cache, and carry no crash or idempotency surface\n35|// of their own; crash/idempotency evidence for the story is the secconftest\n36|// Transactor battery, which CI executes but which lives outside this package.\n37|// Availability is evaluated on the host that runs the check: a positive claim\n38|// about a capability available here is admitted even when the same sentence\n39|// would be refused on a host where the probe fails. Cross-host claim truth is\n40|// outside this gate. The advertisement scanner matches only backticked\n41|// capability IDs, never bare prose: an advertisement that names a\n42|// capability without backticks — however positive its verbs — is not\n43|// checked and is admitted. The scanner reads backticked prose only; it\n44|// classifies sentences, not intent, and any backticked sentence it cannot\n45|// classify is refused rather than ignored.\n46|//\n47|// Deliberate shape decision: this package ships no main package. Its library\n48|// entry points import internal/secconftest for the probe vocabulary, and\n49|// secconftest reads internal/specdoc, which the specdoc guard forbids any new\n50|// main from reaching (TestEmbeddedDocumentNeverReachesAProductBinary and\n51|// TestModuleHasNoProductCommandYet). A cigate command would need either a\n52|// foreign allowlist widening or a second probe vocabulary, both of which this\n53|// story exists to refuse. CI therefore drives these gates through focused,\n54|// name-guarded go test selections; the guards prove the selection matched.\n55|package cigate"}}}
