{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b60-5dda-7951-9c64-98cc389b396d"},"sequence":320,"recorded_at":1780531400000635,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"40ff76d8-c4c8-496c-8b60-7c2779b89e32"},"task_id":"40ff76d8-c4c8-496c-8b60-7c2779b89e32","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"40ff76d8-c4c8-496c-8b60-7c2779b89e32","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2uowwk/TASK-260830-2uowwk_review-verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2uowwk — review verdict, CR revision 2 (`story_final`)\n2|\n3|**Verdict: accepted → `accept_cr` → `integrating`.**\n4|**repeat-of: none.** All five rev1 blocking findings (F1–F5) and the verb-battery\n5|observation are closed and independently re-measured. The residue below is four\n6|mechanism-claim inaccuracies and one unmeasured region, none of which lets a gate\n7|admit what its stated contract forbids; each is a one-line or one-test fix and is\n8|itemised for a follow-up leaf.\n9|\n10|Reviewed tree `8d8231ac0ae2ba557f4c02d0c88b9f905a19821a` (== CR candidate),\n11|base `157a54cfe4e952a2638b574230967989178e9a05`. Tree OID re-derived from the\n12|working tree through a temp `GIT_INDEX_FILE` **before and after** every probe:\n13|both times equal to the record. 50 of the 60 CR paths carry 0 bytes of diff\n14|against `HEAD`; this leaf is the 10 files below.\n15|\n16|Environment: darwin/arm64, go1.25.5, in the Story worktree.\n17|\n18|---\n19|\n20|## G-A — did F1's deletion leave a hole? No.\n21|\n22|| Probe | Result |\n23|| --- | --- |\n24|| `grep -c 'Record live probe verdicts' ci.yml` | **0** — step deleted, not reworded |\n25|| `grep -c 'live probe' ci.yml` | **0** (the sole surviving mention is the comment at :298) |\n26|| What now establishes AC row 11 | `capability-claims` job → `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim`, name-guarded by a `^--- PASS:` grep loop over all six selected tests. Ran the step verbatim: exit 0, **6 of 6 PASS guards** matched |\n27|| README + doc.go describe the design | Yes — both say \"with every probe forced unavailable\", not live scanning |\n28|| Is `ProbeState.Available` still dead? | **No.** `claims.go:235` reads it (`availability[state.ID] = state.Available`); both postures are driven — `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim` (all false) and `TestRealREADMEAdmitsWhenAllAvailable` (all true). What remains discarded is the **live probe outcome**: `ProbeStates()` has no caller but `CapabilityIDs()`, which drops availability. `doc.go` states this correctly; `ci.yml:298` and `LOGBOOK` 2249 do not — see finding R1 |\n29|\n30|Gate-defeat probe on the real README (planted, then restored byte-identical):\n31|a backticked flat positive claim is **REFUSED** with reason\n32|`positive availability claim for an unavailable capability`.\n33|\n34|## G-B — F3's wiring is real in both directions\n35|\n36|`TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation` ties CI's `go test -list` leg to\n37|`cigate.FuzzTargets()`. I mutated both sides of the tie:\n38|\n39|| Mutant | Result |\n40|| --- | --- |\n41|| add `FuzzZZReviewProbeUnmapped` to `secconftest/fuzz_test.go`, no `FuzzTargetEntry` | **FAIL** — `listed targets = [… FuzzZZReviewProbeUnmapped], derivation = […]` |\n42|| remove `\"FuzzDetectCaseCollision\"` from `FuzzTargetEntry`, target still present | **FAIL** — same test, mirrored message |\n43|\n44|Both restored byte-identical (`diff -r` against a pre-probe copy of\n45|`internal/secconftest`; `git status` clean).\n46|\n47|Derivation scope, measured rather than read: `FuzzTargets()` derives\n48|**secconftest only** (8, from the instrument's own map). `canonicaljson` (4) and\n49|`scalar` (1) own no entry map and are derived per package by CI's own `-list`,\n50|pinned by the total count. Live `-list` returns 8 + 4 + 1 = **13**, matching the\n51|pin. A package CI cannot scan fails closed: `go test ./pkg -list` is a bare\n52|command under `set -e`, so a compile or resolution failure aborts the step.\n53|\n54|## G-C — F5's new packages, fail-closed and per-target budget\n55|\n56|**Empty inner result.** The `grep '^Fuzz' … | sed … >> file` pipeline takes\n57|`sed`'s status, so `set -e` does **not** fire on a package with zero targets. I\n58|built a three-package replica: package B empty → loop completes, `test -s`\n59|passes, and the run dies at `test \"$(wc -l …)\" -eq 13` with **exit 1**. So the\n60|step is fail-closed — via the count pin, not via the grep. `ci.yml:240-241`\n61|claims otherwise; see finding R2.\n62|\n63|**Per-target budget, and no stdin theft.** Ran the smoke loop verbatim. The\n64|`while read` body runs `go test`, which is the classic shape that eats the\n65|remaining lines of the redirected list. It does not here: **13 of 13 iterations\n66|executed**, 13 per-target logs produced, all 13 carrying `^fuzz: elapsed`,\n67|18s total. Each target gets its own `-fuzztime=100x`.\n68|\n69|**Stated-bound-worthy fact (R5).** In 5 of 13 targets the 100x budget is spent\n70|entirely on baseline-corpus coverage and the engine never reaches the mutation\n71|phase (`now fuzzing with N workers` absent): `secconftest/FuzzRedactCorpus`\n72|(103-entry corpus) and all four `canonicaljson` targets (196 entries). The\n73|README's claim for this job — \"Every derived target executed its engine, proven\n74|by its elapsed line\" — is **accurate** and does not overclaim mutation. Worth\n75|stating, not a defect.\n76|\n77|## G-D — verb-drop census: kills are behavioural, bookkeeping is gone\n78|\n79|Rev1's `claims_test.go:57` size `Fatalf` aborted the parent before any subtest.\n80|Re-censused every row from scratch:\n81|\n82|| Battery | Rows | Subtests that fire under each drop | Killed by its own subtest |\n83|| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n84|| `positiveAvailability` | 5 | **7 of 7** every time | **5 of 5** |\n85|| `negations` | 13 | **14 of 14** every time | **13 of 13**, one-to-one, no cross-cover |\n86|\n87|Census direction, which is the half a drop battery cannot prove:\n88|\n89|| Mutant | Result |\n90|| --- | --- |\n91|| add gate verb `operational` with no claim row | `battery-covers-gate` **FAIL** — `gate verb \"operational\" has no claim row` |\n92|| add gate negation `except` with no row | `battery-covers-gate` **FAIL** — `gate negation \"except\" has no conditional row` |\n93|\n94|Under a verb drop the census stays green and only the behavioural row reddens —\n95|the kill mechanism is behaviour, not table size.\n96|\n97|## G-E — the Story is landable on merit\n98|\n99|| Check | Result |\n100|| --- | --- |\n101|| `origin/main` | `157a54cfe4e952a2638b574230967989178e9a05` — **equals the CR base** |\n102|| fast-forward | `origin/main` is an ancestor of `HEAD`; **2 ahead, 0 behind** |\n103|| signatures | `722ed1a` and `7f90e58` both `Good \"git\" signature for oparin@me.com` (ECDSA `SHA256:V6JiKG…`). The third leaf commit does not exist yet — this CR is uncommitted working-tree work by design |\n104|| frozen leaves | `git diff 722ed1a -- internal/secprim` → **0 bytes**; `git diff 7f90e58 -- internal/secconftest` → **0 bytes** |\n105|| branch protection on `main` | none (`404 Branch not protected`) — the old `verify` job's disappearance cannot strand a required check |\n106|| action resolution | `actions/checkout@v7` + `actions/setup-go@v7` unchanged from `HEAD` and green on `main` at `157a54cf` today |\n107|| first-run risk | **the workflow triggers on `pull_request`**, so the Story PR is the first hosted execution of all nine new jobs, not `main`. A macOS/Linux divergence reddens the PR, not trunk |\n108|| workflow structure | 10 jobs; `gates-verdict.needs` covers **all 9** non-verdict jobs exactly (no missing, no extra); `timeout-minutes` on 10 of 10; exactly one `if:` in the file (`always()` on `gates-verdict`) |\n109|| aggregator | drove the `jq` over synthetic states: `success`→admit; `skipped`/`failure`/`cancelled`→**reject**. `{}` admits, unreachable because `needs` is static and complete |\n110|\n111|**Stated bound (R6): Linux execution is unverified, not inferred.** No container\n112|runtime exists on this host (no docker/colima/podman; lima has no instance), so I\n113|could not execute the ubuntu legs. `internal/secprim` and `internal/secconftest`\n114|have never run on a hosted Linux runner — both leaf commits are unlanded. Static\n115|mitigation only: `open_member_unix.go:84-97` handles both `ELOOP` (Linux) and\n116|`ENOTDIR` (Darwin) for the same O_NOFOLLOW event, and `task-board.config.json`\n117|already carries `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...`. I report this as\n118|**unknown**; the PR run resolves it before any trunk push.\n119|\n120|## Not charged to this CR — confirmed recorded, not silently fixed\n121|\n122|- `//go:generate` → `// go:generate` defeats catalog freshness with the token\n123|  preserved. `internal/catalog` carries **0 bytes** of diff against the CR base,\n124|  and the freshness step is **byte-identical** to `HEAD`'s. Recorded in the\n125|  outcome doc (bound 7) and `LOGBOOK` 2249. ✔\n126|- **Additional inherited defeat, not previously named.**\n127|  `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` (`internal/traceability/traceability_test.go`,\n128|  outside this CR's 60 paths) is a `bytes.Contains` gate over `ci.yml`. I moved\n129|  `go vet ./...` from its `run:` step into a YAML comment: the test still\n130|  **PASSES**. It is doubly blind here — `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` contains the\n131|  same substring, so deleting the plain Vet step entirely is invisible to it.\n132|  Pre-existing at `HEAD` (both lines existed there); recording it beside the\n133|  `go:generate` one.\n134|\n135|## G-F — battery provenance\n136|\n137|Document tree OID == record tree OID == my independent derivation. Producer\n138|reports 30 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL, 28 killed, 2 bounded\n139|survivors, narrowing and arm-deletion tabled separately. **I re-ran 29 of the 30\n140|myself** and every one reproduced:\n141|\n142|| Class | Mutants | Result |\n143|| --- | ---: | --- |\n144|| verb drops | 5 | KILLED, each in its own subtest |\n145|| negation drops | 13 | KILLED, each in its own subtest |\n146|| N3 boundary-drop (substring match) | 1 | KILLED — `TestSubstringIsNotAMarker` |\n147|| B1 backtick-widen | 1 | KILLED — `TestUnbacktickedProseIsOutsideTheScanner` + `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim` |\n148|| N5 case-narrow | 1 | KILLED — `/capital` and `/no` |\n149|| N4 version-order-blind | 1 | KILLED — `TestCheckAgreementRefusals/version_order_changed` |\n150|| E1 entry-drop | 1 | KILLED — `TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation` |\n151|| A1–A4, A6 arm deletions | 5 | KILLED |\n152|| A5 target guards | 1 | my deletion variant COMPILE_FAILs (unused import/var); ran **A5c**, dropping the empty-derivation guard → KILLED (`TestSortedTargetsRefusals`) |\n153|| C1 release order swap | 1 | SURVIVED — matches the stated order-is-presentation bound |\n154|\n155|Ratio on the production-derived denominator: **28 killed / 30 applied**, the two\n156|survivors bounded. Denominator is the production lists themselves (5 verbs +\n157|13 negations), both matcher narrowings, case folding, version ordering, every\n158|refusal arm — not a test-side inventory.\n159|\n160|### Seven reviewer-authored mutants the battery did not contain\n161|\n162|| Mutant | Result |\n163|| --- | --- |\n164|| X2 emit only the first finding per sentence | KILLED — `TestMixedAvailabilityFindsOnlyUnavailable` |\n165|| A5c drop the empty-derivation guard | KILLED — `TestSortedTargetsRefusals` |\n166|| **X1 collapse `splitSentences` to paragraph granularity** | **SURVIVED** — see R4 |\n167|| X3 drop `nonClaimMarkers` from the unclassified arm | SURVIVED (stricter direction) — see R3 |\n168|| X4 drop `sort.Strings(mentioned)` | SURVIVED — order/presentation, same class as C2 |\n169|| X5 drop the empty-capability guard in `ProbeStates` | SURVIVED — defensive guard whose trigger is unreachable; unmeasured |\n170|\n171|---\n172|\n173|## Findings — none blocking; all itemised for a follow-up leaf\n174|\n175|### R1 — `ci.yml:298` and `LOGBOOK` 2249 state a field is dead that the gate reads\n176|\n177|Both say *\"`ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site.\"* `claims.go:235`\n178|consumes it, and it is the whole input to the availability map. The true and\n179|useful statement is `doc.go`'s: *live probe outcomes* are read by no call site.\n180|A maintainer trusting the comment could delete the field and break the gate.\n181|**Fix:** one word — say \"live probe outcomes\", as `doc.go` already does.\n182|\n183|### R2 — `ci.yml:240-241` names the wrong guard as fail-closed\n184|\n185|*\"An empty derivation fails the grep and the explicit size check alike.\"* The\n186|grep sits in a pipeline, so its exit status is discarded and `set -e` never\n187|fires — proved with a three-package replica where the empty package sailed past\n188|both the grep and `test -s` and died only at the count pin. The step **is**\n189|fail-closed; the comment misattributes it, and a maintainer \"simplifying\" away\n190|the count pin would open exactly the silent-empty hole this job exists to close.\n191|**Fix:** name the count pin as the guard.\n192|\n193|### R3 — the marker census measures occurrence, not effect: markers classify 0 of 2\n194|\n195|Measured on the real README with the production splitter and matchers:\n196|\n197|| Datum | Value |\n198|| --- | ---: |\n199|| sentences mentioning a backticked capability ID | **2** |\n200|| refused as a positive claim | 0 |\n201|| admitted by the **negation** arm | **2** |\n202|| admitted by the **marker** arm | **0** |\n203|| refused as unclassified | 0 |\n204|\n205|`nonClaimMarkers` — 20 words — classifies nothing, which X3 confirms\n206|independently: removing the entire list from the gate changes no test outcome.\n207|`TestEveryNonClaimMarkerOccursInCorpus` passes only because README line 659 is\n208|one long sentence containing 18 of the 20 marker words, with line 968 supplying\n209|`rejected` and `scan`. Its own comment says it exists so that \"a marker that\n210|fires on no real sentence\" cannot survive as \"an admission hole waiting for\n211|future text\" — that is precisely the current state, and the test does not see it.\n212|This also makes the README gate row's *\"every backticked capability mention\n213|resolves to probe, skip, gate, or test context\"* false as a mechanism claim:\n214|0 of 2 resolve that way; 2 of 2 resolve via negations.\n215|**Fix:** assert the classifying *arm* per mention, not word occurrence; correct\n216|the README cell to say mentions resolve to a **negated or non-claim** context.\n217|\n218|### R4 — a narrowing mutant of the sentence splitter survives the whole suite\n219|\n220|X1 replaces the sentence-terminal boundary with paragraph granularity. The suite\n221|stays green, yet the behaviour is load-bearing in production: the two-sentence\n222|document *\"The `fifo` capability is not available on Linux. The `fifo` capability\n223|is available on Windows.\"* is **REFUSED** today and would be **ADMITTED** under\n224|X1. `TestFindingCarriesLine` is the only splitter test and it uses two separate\n225|blank-line blocks, so it cannot see the change.\n226|**Fix:** one row pinning that exact two-sentence document.\n227|\n228|### R5 / R6 — stated bounds\n229|\n230|R5: 5 of 13 fuzz targets never leave baseline-corpus gathering at `-fuzztime=100x`\n231|(measured above). The README does not overclaim; state the bound.\n232|R6: Linux execution unverified on this host (measured absence of any container\n233|runtime, reported as unknown rather than inferred).\n234|\n235|### Adjudicated, not re-litigated\n236|\n237|Five flat positive claims that also carry an incidental negation token are\n238|admitted: `\"The `fifo` capability is available on Windows with no extra setup.\"`\n239|and the `only` / `without` / `not` / `never` variants (5 of 5 admitted; the same\n240|sentence without the negation token is refused). This is the same class the rev1\n241|verdict examined under F4 rows 4–6 and placed inside `doc.go`'s stated bound\n242|*\"it classifies sentences, not intent\"*. I reproduce it with more mundane\n243|sentences and record it here; I do not re-open it as a finding.\n244|\n245|---\n246|\n247|## Suites re-run on the candidate tree, this session\n248|\n249|| Command | Exit | Evidence |\n250|| --- | ---: | --- |\n251|| `go test ./... -v -count=1` | 0 | 22 `^ok`, 0 `^FAIL`, **1354 `--- PASS`**, 1 `--- SKIP` (`TestDumpSweepSites`) |\n252|| `go test -race ./... -count=1` | 0 | 22 `^ok`, **0 `DATA RACE`** |\n253|| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 | 22 `coverage:` lines, 0 `no test files`; **cigate 90.5%**, secprim 94.4%, secconftest 92.6% |\n254|| `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` | 0 | clean |\n255|| `GOOS=windows go vet ./...`, `GOOS=windows go build ./...` | 0 | clean |\n256|| `gofmt -l internal` | 0 | 339 files scanned, empty list |\n257|| `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 | contracts=60, compatibility=55, cases=94 — unchanged |\n258|| `go generate ./internal/catalog` + `git diff --exit-code` | 0 | clean |\n259|| contract-preservation step verbatim | 0 | **6 of 6** `--- PASS` guards matched |\n260|| capability-claims step verbatim | 0 | **6 of 6** `--- PASS` guards matched |\n261|| fuzz target-derivation step verbatim | 0 | **2 of 2** `--- PASS` guards matched |\n262|| fixture matrix, darwin leg `internal/secprim` | 0 | 51 `--- PASS`, 0 `--- SKIP` |\n263|| fixture matrix, darwin leg `internal/secconftest` | 0 | 59 `--- PASS`, 0 `--- SKIP` |\n264|| fuzz-smoke derive + smoke, verbatim | 0 | 13 targets, 13 iterations, 13 `fuzz: elapsed` |\n265|\n266|`-race`, `-cover` and per-package coverage match the producer's `verify-rev2.log`.\n267|\n268|## Tree integrity\n269|\n270|Every mutant was applied to a pre-probe copy and restored by copy-back, never by\n271|`git checkout`. After the final probe: `diff -r` clean on `internal/cigate` and\n272|`internal/secconftest`, `cmp` clean on `README.md` and `.github/workflows/ci.yml`,\n273|`git status --short` back to the exact three `M` + one `??`, and the re-derived\n274|tree OID equal to `8d8231ac0ae2ba557f4c02d0c88b9f905a19821a`.\n275|\n276|## AC coverage\n277|\n278|**11 of 11 rows driven**, each with a named committed test and a production call\n279|site. I independently drove rows 1–2 (contract gates), 3 (vet/gofmt), 4 (race),\n280|5 (coverage), 6 (fixture matrix darwin legs + fuzz derivation + smoke), 7 and 11\n281|(capability-claims step plus a planted-claim defeat probe), and read rows 8–10\n282|against their named tests in the frozen leaves."}}}
