{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c65b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b60-5dda-7951-9c64-98cc389b396d"},"sequence":392,"recorded_at":1780531400000779,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"5a2dfd08-d46d-4c99-a109-9bf17a0bf8d5"},"task_id":"5a2dfd08-d46d-4c99-a109-9bf17a0bf8d5","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"5a2dfd08-d46d-4c99-a109-9bf17a0bf8d5","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-17-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"2249\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head; echo ===; sed -n '100,180p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Inspect LOGBOOK claim context\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"131:### 2249 — CI gates leaf round 2: five review findings closed, all claims reproduce\\n===\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 98 acceptance cases). Battery: 22 applied / 21 killed / 1 survived (M12 declared equivalent per N5) + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct control rows; all 4 token-preserving killed behaviourally with zero census kill.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2252 — review round 3: saturation short-circuit reclassified malformed versions (G1)\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (G1 blocking + N1–N3 notes; F1/F2/F4/F5 and the F3 rewrite stand as the reviewer verified them and were not re-litigated). Production: `provhost/protocol.go` `parseMajor` only — the saturating early `return math.MaxInt, true` is now `major = math.MaxInt; continue`, so an overflowing first component still saturates but the minor/patch shape check always runs. Doc paragraph narrowed to what the code enforces (only a fully numeric X.Y.Z reports a recognized major). Tests: new `TestParseMajorSaturationStillValidatesTheRest` (5 giant-malformed rows assert `parseMajor` unrecognized AND `DecodeResponse` provider_protocol_error/exit 13 through the production entry).\\n- FINDING (measured through `DecodeResponse`, pre-fix probe): `99999999999999999999.abc.def`, `99999999999999999999.0.x`, `18446744073709551618..0` classified `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6 while `2.abc.def` classified `provider_protocol_error`/exit 13 — a plugin chose the refusal class and exit status, and the whole provhost suite passed identically on both behaviors (effect census, not branch census: the parse-arm census enumerates rejection branches and cannot see inputs moving between existing arms). Post-fix measurement: all-numeric giants (`18446744073709551618.0.0`, `99999999999999999999.0.0`) stay `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6 — that 13→6 shift is the intended, still-measured F2 effect; every malformed-rest giant is back to exit 13.\\n- CORRECTION: the round-2 outcome sentence \\\"no gate was weakened … parse-arm census derives the identical set\\\" is withdrawn as classification-stability evidence in `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round3.md`; the census claim survives only in its scoped form (saturation adds no `return 0, false` branch, so the inventory needs no new row). AC ratio corrected to 14 of 15 driven + 1 stated bound (row 14, F6 future-caller prose). N2 bound stated: the attestation tripwire matches `CallExpr` only, so a function-value binding would be missed (0 such references today). Battery scripts live at repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/` (N3).\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round3.md` on the board task (G1 table, corrected arm-shift sentence, 14+1 AC ratio, 8-mutant battery table); battery script `mutG1_round3.py` + `mutsG1_round3.json` under repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/`.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race` provider/provhost/terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 98 acceptance cases). Battery on the 6-obligation parseMajor denominator: 8 applied / 8 killed / 0 survivors (narrowing 4/4 incl. the round-2 shape, arm-deletion 2/2, census-only 2/2 incl. a token-preserving collapse) + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct control rows.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2251 — review round 2: two wrapping bounds gates, fail-open lift arm, false-fact bound, blind census\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (F1–F5 blocking, F6–F7 notes). Production: `terminalbackend/descriptor.go` (early bound refusal in `descriptorGeometry`), `terminalbackend.go` (`semverMajor` saturates), `provhost/protocol.go` (`parseMajor` saturates, no new census branch), `provider/lift.go` (default arm fail-closed: unregistered → registry refusal, registered-no-arm → input handed back, never a wire object). Docs: provhost `doc.go`/`identity.go` bounds rewritten, descriptor future-caller paragraph. Tests: overflow vectors (F1/F2), registered-no-arm refusal (F4), §5.5 verify measurement + attestation tripwire (F3), whole-package multi-form derivation + 4 plants (F5), v3-error DecodeBound premise proof.\\n- FINDING (measured, not inferred): `VerifyObjectIdentity` on the pinned §5.5 example returns the claimed `record_id` with nil error — the example IS the true omit-self digest, so the old bound's justification was false; rewritten around the true deferral (admission contract includes non-recomputed digests; mismatched-live-binding ruling belongs to the identity owner). `VerifyObjectIdentity` has 0 production call sites repo-wide (AST scan over 125 files in `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`).\\n- FINDING: `provider` refusal inventory forbids `errors.New`/`fmt.Errorf`/`panic` outside `os_unix.go`/`os_windows.go`, so the F4 fix returns the input failure itself for registered-no-arm codes — no new construction site, audit untouched.\\n- FINDING: saturating (not unrecognizing) huge majors keeps the provhost parse-arm census stable (no new `return 0, false` branch) and routes 2^64+2 to `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6 instead of the exit-13 unusable-frame arm.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome.md` updated on the board task (15/15 AC rows with call sites; battery 26 applied / 26 killed / 0 survivors + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL controls as distinct rows; candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`).\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race` on provider/provhost/terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, catalog current, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 98 acceptance cases).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2250 — v3 envelope owner named (terminalbackend), provider error lift built\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y (second leaf of STORY-260905-3t31e9; advisories A3/A4 + carried F3). New: `terminalbackend/descriptor.go` (closed §7.A descriptor parse + `AdmitProviderDescriptor`), `provider/lift.go` (`Lift`); edited: provhost protocol/doc/identity comments + derived error contract, provider doc, 7.A registry group + digest, terminalbackend inventory rows. Leaf-1 production untouched.\\n- DECISION: §7.A owner is terminalbackend, not provhost. Provhost cannot admit 3.0.0 transport: our host writes v2 requests and §7.A sends v2/v3 mismatches down the §15.1 close/termination rule, so admission would trust a foreign major and redden the pinned `3.0.0 → incompatible_protocol` gates. Refusal is the specified outcome; the dual-stack host (v3 requests + descriptor carriage + 1.3.0 decode) is a follow-up specified in the outcome, not a silent scope.\\n- DECISION: `provider.Error` keeps machine-local facts for logs; the wire message is rebuilt from the stable code alone by `Lift` (static text, empty details, cause local-only). Constructor restructuring would not remove the rebuild need, so the seam is the lift, documented in `provider/doc.go`.\\n- FINDING: `git stash create -u` trees omit untracked files — verify candidate trees with `git ls-tree`. The recorded tree OID was built via a detached index (`GIT_INDEX_FILE` copy + `add -A` + `write-tree`) with blob hashes checked against worktree bytes.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome.md` on the board task (11/11 AC rows with call sites, 19-row mutant table, gates with exit codes, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`).\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race` exit 0, `-cover` exit 0, `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, catalog current, `tracecheck` ok. Battery 17 applied / 17 killed / 0 survivors (+ NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL controls). Fuzz smoke not run (targets in untouched packages; CI runs it).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2249 — CI gates leaf round 2: five review findings closed, all claims reproduce\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2uowwk rework (review-verdict-rev1, F1–F5 blocking + verb-battery observation). `internal/cigate` + `.github/workflows/ci.yml` + README. `internal/secprim` + `internal/secconftest` production untouched (restored byte-identical after two probe mutants; `git status` clean on both).\\n- F1: deleted the `Record live probe verdicts` step — it ran a synthetic-verdict test and grepped a constant line through a non-gating pipe. CI now scans the README with every probe forced unavailable (stronger than live scanning, host-independent); README table and `cigate/doc.go` say so, and the workflow comment states `ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site.\\n- F3: wired, not deleted. New `TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation` holds `go test -list ^Fuzz` output equal to `FuzzTargets()`; CI's fuzz-smoke runs it name-guarded before smoking. Entry-drop mutant kills both the derivation test and `TestFuzzDriversReachProduction`.\\n- F5: fuzz-smoke now derives per package over `secconftest` + `canonicaljson` + `scalar` (8+4+1=13, count pinned), each smoked with the `^fuzz: elapsed` guard — all 13 observed locally. `doc.go` no longer claims entry points stay in one package.\\n- F4: backtick bound stated in `doc.go` Stated bounds and the README row, pinned by `TestUnbacktickedProseIsOutsideTheScanner` (bare-prose positive claims admitted). Backtick-widening mutant killed by that test and by the real-README gate (bare `fifo` in prose gets refused).\\n- BATTERY: verb/negation size `Fatalf`s replaced by per-row behavioural kills + `battery-covers-gate` censuses. Three rewritten negation rows (`n't`, `pending`, `unless`) each previously hid behind a second negation. Censused drops: 5/5 verbs and 13/13 negations kill in their own subtest (spot-verified `supported`, `pending`; `available` also trips `TestFindingCarriesLine` by shared sentence).\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-2uowwk_ci-gates.md` rev2 (11/11 AC rows, 30-mutant battery, per-job red proofs) + `TASK-260830-2uowwk_mutants-rev2.log` + `TASK-260830-2uowwk_verify-rev2.log`. Full suite 22 ok, `-race` 22 ok, `-cover` 22 lines (cigate 90.5%), vet both GOOS, gofmt, catalog freshness, `tracecheck` all exit 0.\\n- NOTE (pre-existing, not fixed here): catalog-freshness step defeated by `//go:generate` → `// go:generate` (token preserved); at HEAD before this leaf. The contract-version gate still catches version drift with the directive disarmed.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2248 — CI gates leaf: cigate library, ten-job workflow, no new main\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2uowwk (final leaf of STORY-260830-1i3qu7). New `internal/cigate` (doc/contracts/claims/targets + 3 test files, no `main`); `.github/workflows/ci.yml` 1 job → 10; README \\\"Continuous Conformance Gates (CI)\\\" section. `internal/secprim` + `internal/secconftest` production untouched; no foreign guard weakened.\\n- DECISION: no new `main` package. First Rosewood `cmd/cigate` tripped `TestEmbeddedDocumentNeverReachesAProductBinary` + `TestModuleHasNoProductCommandYet` (lib reaches specdoc via secconftest). Widening that allowlist would self-mint an exemption, so the command was deleted; CI drives gates through focused name-guarded `go test -run` selections instead. Recorded in `internal/cigate/doc.go`.\\n- FINDING: `go test -fuzz='^NoSuch$'` exits 0 (\\\"no fuzz tests to fuzz\\\"). Fuzz-smoke step therefore requires the `^fuzz: elapsed` line per target, proven both directions (real 0, bogus 1).\\n- FINDING: existing `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` pins four literals in ci.yml; the rewrite initially dropped `go build ./...` and used non-verbose test. Restored: native Build step + `go test ./... -v -count=1`. The guard worked as designed.\\n- FINDING: N3-v1 mutant (drop one marker) survived — marker arm has redundancy by construction, not a hole. Replaced with boundary-anchoring narrowing (substring match), killed by new `TestSubstringIsNotAMarker`.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-2uowwk_ci-gates.md` (11/11 AC rows, 13-row mutant table, per-job red proofs with exit codes) + `TASK-260830-2uowwk_mutants.log`.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race ./...` exit 0 (22 ok x3 sweeps), `-cover` exit 0 (22 lines, cigate 90.5%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (60/55 contracts, unchanged). Mutants 13 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL, 11 killed (5 narrowing + 6 arm-deletion), 2 census survivors with bounds (order-only).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2155 — secconftest round-3 rework: crashed commit counts as committed, Require wiring pinned, LOGBOOK corrected\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c round-3 (review-verdict-rev2, C1/C1b/C2/C2b blocking + 7 unbounded survivors). Production (test instrument) only in `internal/secconftest`: `crash.go` (commit-apply fault finalizes with parked receipt, `ErrPreparePastFinalize`/`ErrCommitPastFinalize`, rollback forgets, staged-missing naming), `skip.go` (`requireT` interface), `main_test.go` (new, `TestMain` final report), `doc.go` (terminal + wiring bounds). Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` untouched.\\n- C1 RULE: a crashed commit counts as committed — the durable write already happened, so rollback is forbidden (`ErrRollbackPastFinalize`) and bytes survive; recovery is via `CommittedBytes`/operator. Driven by `TestTransactorCrashedCommitIsFinal`. C1b neighbours all named (no ENOENT inheritance): rollback-twice, commit-twice, commit-after-rollback, prepare-after-commit refused; prepare-after-rollback restages. Fifth crash point armed through the Transactor (P7 closed).\\n- C2b: `TestRequireSkipArmRecordsVerdict`/`TestRequireFailArmRecordsVerdict` drive the real `Require` through both arms with a recording fake (M04/M05 killed); `TestMain` prints counters after the parallel tests. Round-2's two untrue sentences superseded in the round-3 outcome doc.\\n- C2: 2035 entry corrected in place (false counts withdrawn, digest kept, correction note added); worktree sweep clean.\\n- SURVIVORS CLOSED: M02 (empty-ID with probe), M08 (symlink strictness pinned exactly), M16 (empty operation ID), M27 (whitespace-quote message pin) — all killed. Battery re-derived from this tree: 38 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL / 0 VET_FAIL, 36 killed (narrowing 26 + arm-deletion 6 + census-only 4), 2 survived with bounds: N-DriveRedactNoDelegate (N16 delegation bound) and S1-ModeBitsFalse (survive-as-SKIP). Token-preserving mutant ran the full suite. Manifest `c6018721…` identical after the battery.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round3.md` (6/6 AC rows, 38-row mutant table, gates with exit codes) + `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_mutant-battery-round3.log` + full-test log.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), secconftest `-race` exit 0, `./... -cover` exit 0 (secconftest 92.6%, secprim 94.4%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged), 8/8 fuzz `-fuzztime=100x` exit 0 with no corpus written, verbose 246 PASS / 0 SKIP / 0 FAIL, digest `5569f34caab734eb`.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2105 — secconftest round-2 rework: C1–C4 closed, instrument stops reporting untrue things\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c round-2 (review-verdict-rev1, C1–C4 blocking). Production (test instrument) only in `internal/secconftest`: `crash.go` (finalize gate + `ErrRollbackPastFinalize`, `RemainingArmed`), `skip.go` (`Report()` over live counters, real `mkfifo` fifo probe), `skip_fifo_unix/windows.go` (new, `makeFifo` + fault seam), `hostile.go` untouched, `fuzz_test.go` (no-op poles), `doc.go` (bounds). Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` untouched (`git diff HEAD -- internal/secprim` empty).\\n- C1: `Rollback` now refuses post-commit with `ErrRollbackPastFinalize` and leaves committed bytes intact; `TestTransactorRefusesRollbackPastFinalize` commits-then-rolls-back (the arm it is named for) plus both old arms. Deleting the gate is killed by it (battery A1).\\n- C2: `Report()` reads the live counters; `TestSkipReportReadsRecordedVerdicts` records synthetic verdicts, asserts the report moves, restores state (gutting `recordVerdict` reddens it, battery A4). The round-1 `skipped=0` citation was a constant — genuine datum is 0 `--- SKIP` / 0 `--- FAIL` lines under `go test -v` on darwin non-root, now cited i