`TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round3.md` (6/6 AC rows, 38-row mutant table, gates with exit codes) + `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_mutant-battery-round3.log` + full-test log.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), secconftest `-race` exit 0, `./... -cover` exit 0 (secconftest 92.6%, secprim 94.4%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged), 8/8 fuzz `-fuzztime=100x` exit 0 with no corpus written, verbose 246 PASS / 0 SKIP / 0 FAIL, digest `5569f34caab734eb`.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2105 — secconftest round-2 rework: C1–C4 closed, instrument stops reporting untrue things\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c round-2 (review-verdict-rev1, C1–C4 blocking). Production (test instrument) only in `internal/secconftest`: `crash.go` (finalize gate + `ErrRollbackPastFinalize`, `RemainingArmed`), `skip.go` (`Report()` over live counters, real `mkfifo` fifo probe), `skip_fifo_unix/windows.go` (new, `makeFifo` + fault seam), `hostile.go` untouched, `fuzz_test.go` (no-op poles), `doc.go` (bounds). Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` untouched (`git diff HEAD -- internal/secprim` empty).\\n- C1: `Rollback` now refuses post-commit with `ErrRollbackPastFinalize` and leaves committed bytes intact; `TestTransactorRefusesRollbackPastFinalize` commits-then-rolls-back (the arm it is named for) plus both old arms. Deleting the gate is killed by it (battery A1).\\n- C2: `Report()` reads the live counters; `TestSkipReportReadsRecordedVerdicts` records synthetic verdicts, asserts the report moves, restores state (gutting `recordVerdict` reddens it, battery A4). The round-1 `skipped=0` citation was a constant — genuine datum is 0 `--- SKIP` / 0 `--- FAIL` lines under `go test -v` on darwin non-root, now cited in README/outcome/doc.go.\\n- C3: fifo probe builds a real FIFO (`syscall.Mkfifo`+Lstat; Windows stub unavailable) with a fault seam (`TestSkipFifoProbeAttemptsItsCapability` kills a success-on-failure weakening, battery N14). All 4 probes gate real tests: symlink→escape witness, fifo→byte-exchange fixture, mode-bits+nonroot→denial test (4/4 wired, was 1/4).\\n- C4: all 8 listed survivors closed — digest report/name distinguishing tests (N1–N3), bidi rune-for-rune pin + corpus coverage (N4–N5), Gate pin+drive for all 18 classes (N6), verdict counter test (A4), commit-requires-prepare with planted staged file (A3). Battery re-derived from this tree: 29 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL / 0 VET_FAIL, 27 killed (15 narrowing + 8 arm-deletion + 4 census-only), 2 survived with bounds: N16 driver-delegation (read-verified + arrival-counted) and S1 mode-bits-false (survives-as-SKIP by construction — the SKIP line is the signal). N10 token-preserving mutant killed by the full behavioral suite; tree sha256-identical after the battery.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round2.md` (6/6 AC rows corrected, 29-row mutant table with bounds, gates with exit codes) + `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_mutant-battery-round2.log` + full-test log.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), secconftest `-race` exit 0, `./... -cover` exit 0 (secconftest 89.3%, secprim 94.4% unchanged), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged), 8/8 fuzz `-fuzztime=100x` exit 0 with no corpus written, digest `5569f34caab734eb` x5 processes.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2035 — secconftest instrument leaf: runners, fake clocks, crash points, fuzz, hostile strings, skips\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c (second leaf of STORY-260830-1i3qu7). New package `internal/secconftest` (doc/runner/clock/crash/fuzz/hostile/skip + 6 test files): sorted deterministic Runner with execution digest and zero-call refusal, wall-clock-free Fake with Recording wiring detector, CR-MAT-* Injector over a three-phase Transactor with §13.13 outcomes and idempotency_mismatch, 8 Fuzz targets through one shared Driver with seed arrival proofs, 18-class spec-derived hostile roster plus symlink-escape commit witness, 4 probed capabilities with strict-platform failure. Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` production untouched; `task-board.config.json` gains the 8 required fuzz validation commands (pinned by `TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget`, which failed until registered).\\n- FINDING: the repo already forces fuzz registration — a new Fuzz target without a config line fails `TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget` plus its coverage parent. The instrument therefore cannot silently add unfuzzed-in-CI targets.\\n- FINDING (M6): a Fake leaking `time.Now` is caught by two fresh fakes disagreeing (real timestamps in the failure), not just by the sleep test — the stronger kill.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest.md` (6/6 AC rows with call sites; digest `5569f34caab734eb` x3). CORRECTION (round-3): the mutant counts and the darwin skip citation first written here (10-row table, 10/10 killed, skipped=0) were disproven in round-1 review and are superseded by the round-2 rework entry above and `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round2.md` (29 applied / 2 survivors with bounds; per-test `--- SKIP` lines as the datum).\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), `-race` exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (secconftest 86.9%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged). 8/8 fuzz targets pass 5s smoke and `-fuzztime=100x` with no corpus written.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 1939 — secprim round-3 rework: C1 handle binding, C2 classify-before-close, C3 spelling bound, N24 restored\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 20948,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 5237,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
