{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c79d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b60-5dda-7951-9c64-98cc389b396d"},"sequence":553,"recorded_at":1780531400001101,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"90b907d6-8c13-40b4-9476-770ca3faedab"},"task_id":"90b907d6-8c13-40b4-9476-770ca3faedab","event":{"kind":"started","task_id":"90b907d6-8c13-40b4-9476-770ca3faedab","span_id":"f0dd95952c57da85"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c79f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b60-5dda-7951-9c64-98cc389b396d"},"sequence":554,"recorded_at":1780531400001103,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"90b907d6-8c13-40b4-9476-770ca3faedab"},"task_id":"90b907d6-8c13-40b4-9476-770ca3faedab","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"90b907d6-8c13-40b4-9476-770ca3faedab","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree/README.md`.\n(699 line(s) above)\n700|## Continuous Conformance Gates (CI)\n701|\n702|`.github/workflows/ci.yml` is the gate that decides what a green check\n703|means. Every job proves its selection matched something: a test selector,\n704|file scan, derivation, or matrix expansion that finds nothing fails closed\n705|instead of passing on an empty result set. No job declares a skip\n706|condition, so no job can skip quietly; the terminal verdict job additionally\n707|refuses any skipped, failed, or cancelled dependency.\n708|\n709|| Job | What runs | What green proves |\n710|| --- | --- | --- |\n711|| Contract preservation | `tracecheck`, catalog freshness, focused `internal/cigate` contract gates | The pinned lock and the generated catalog agree on every historical and current contract version, and each gate selection matched its named test |\n712|| Linters | `go vet`, Windows `go vet`, `gofmt` with a non-empty-scan guard | The tree type-checks on both GOOS values and carries no formatting drift |\n713|| Test | Full suite uncached | Every package passed; the run matched at least one package |\n714|| Race detector | Full suite under `-race` | No data race fired anywhere in the suite |\n715|| Coverage numbers | Full suite with `-cover`, percentages in the run summary | Per-package coverage was measured and reported; there is no floor, so coverage is a number, not a gate |\n716|| Conformance fixtures | Story suites on Ubuntu and macOS | Exact fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass per platform, with skip lines as the skip datum; crash/idempotency evidence comes from the Transactor battery in this matrix |\n717|| Fuzz smoke | Targets derived per package from the compiled test binaries (`secconftest`, `canonicaljson`, `scalar`), each smoked briefly; the `secconftest` leg is diffed against the `cigate.FuzzTargets` derivation | Every derived target executed its engine, proven by its elapsed line rather than by exit status alone |\n718|| Unsupported-capability claim check | README scanned with every probe forced unavailable | No unsupported capability is advertised: every backticked capability mention resolves to probe, skip, gate, or test context, never to a positive availability claim about an unavailable capability. Only backticked IDs are scanned — prose without backticks is outside the gate |\n719|| Windows compile-only | `GOOS=windows` build and vet, test files included | The tree compiles for Windows; green here never implies behaviour was executed there |\n720|| Gates verdict | Dependency-result check | Every gate above succeeded and none skipped |\n721|\n722|[`internal/cigate`](internal/cigate) holds the CI-facing gate library:\n723|contract-version agreement derived from `internal/specpin` and\n724|`internal/catalog` (a version either side cannot account for is refused),\n725|secconftest fuzz-target derivation from the instrument's own target map\n726|(held equal to CI's `go test -list` leg, so neither side can drift), and\n727|the advertisement check over the `internal/secconftest` probe vocabulary\n728|with every probe forced unavailable rather than live-read. It ships no command by deliberation: its\n729|library reaches the embedded specification document through the\n730|instrument, which the `specdoc` guard reserves to the existing repository\n731|gates, so CI drives these gates through focused name-guarded test\n732|selections whose guards prove the selection matched.\n733|\n734|## Canonical JSON and Immutable Object Identities\n735|\n736|[`internal/canonicaljson`](internal/canonicaljson) exposes the production RFC\n737|8785 JCS entry point and the AX immutable-object identity calculation. The JCS\n738|path validates I-JSON input before canonicalization, including duplicate-name,\n739|UTF-8, surrogate-pair, ECMAScript number-formatting, string-escaping, and\n740|UTF-16 property-ordering rules. Its number behavior is checked against every\n741|finite RFC 8785 Appendix B sample through the production entry point.\n742|\n743|All four Section 1.6 boundary fixtures that publish a digest are pinned:\n744|`NUM-SAFE-MAX`, `NUM-U64-STRING`, `NUM-U64-MAX`, and `JCS-UTF16-ORDER` are each\n745|recomputed from the production encoder and compared against the value quoted\n746|from `SPEC.md` at the pinned commit, not against a value the implementation\n747|derived for itself.\n748|\n749|The `utf8.ValidString` re-checks in `closed_shapes.go` are kept and documented\n750|rather than deleted; each names `decodeStrict` as the validator that subsumes it.\n751|That subsumption is machine-checked, not only asserted in prose: no exported\n752|function or method may hand an already-decoded value to one of those re-checks,\n753|and `decodeStrict` must remain the only place in the package where bytes become\n754|Go values. Adding a second decoder reddens the pin, as does a map-taking\n755|exported entry point that reaches a re-check by calling it, through the\n756|package's own `immutableObjectShapeValidators` dispatch table, or as a method on\n757|an exported type. All 7 of the 7 derived re-check functions are reachable from\n758|an exported entry point, so none of them is pinned vacuously, and that ratio is\n759|itself asserted rather than left to prose.\n760|\n761|The check is bounded, and the bound is published with it. Its call graph is\n762|derived from the AST, so it models direct calls, calls to methods declared in\n763|the package, and dispatch through a function value; it models nothing about a\n764|callee reached by reflection, by a function value handed to another package, or\n765|through a func-typed struct field. An entry point built one of those ways would\n766|leave the guards live while the pin stayed green — which is why the guards are\n767|kept rather than deleted.\n768|\n769|The AX identity path additionally enforces the Section 1.6 common model: JSON\n770|numbers are integral safe integers, and the exact `schema`/`schema_version`\n771|pair selects the schema-defined self field from the generated catalog bound to\n772|the pinned v0.5.0 source. The catalog contains the reviewed terminal, clone,\n773|registry, and common-object omit-self set, but catalog membership is not a\n774|runtime shape-support claim. A separate explicit shape-validator registry is\n775|checked for exact completeness against every catalog schema/version: a newly\n776|registered identity cannot silently fall through to extension-only\n777|attestation. The public calculation and verification entries currently accept\n778|Session Record `1.0.0`–`3.0.0`, Session Event `1.0.0`–`4.0.0`, Lease,\n779|Checkpoint, Provider Identity, Workspace Group, Blob Descriptor, and Transfer\n(more lines below)"}}}
