m the AST, so it models direct calls, calls to methods declared in\n763|the package, and dispatch through a function value; it models nothing about a\n764|callee reached by reflection, by a function value handed to another package, or\n765|through a func-typed struct field. An entry point built one of those ways would\n766|leave the guards live while the pin stayed green — which is why the guards are\n767|kept rather than deleted.\n768|\n769|The AX identity path additionally enforces the Section 1.6 common model: JSON\n770|numbers are integral safe integers, and the exact `schema`/`schema_version`\n771|pair selects the schema-defined self field from the generated catalog bound to\n772|the pinned v0.5.0 source. The catalog contains the reviewed terminal, clone,\n773|registry, and common-object omit-self set, but catalog membership is not a\n774|runtime shape-support claim. A separate explicit shape-validator registry is\n775|checked for exact completeness against every catalog schema/version: a newly\n776|registered identity cannot silently fall through to extension-only\n777|attestation. The public calculation and verification entries currently accept\n778|Session Record `1.0.0`–`3.0.0`, Session Event `1.0.0`–`4.0.0`, Lease,\n779|Checkpoint, Provider Identity, Workspace Group, Blob Descriptor, and Transfer\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
