{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c94b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b60-5dda-7951-9c64-98cc389b396d"},"sequence":768,"recorded_at":1780531400001531,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a800d573-fdf2-4d37-9bc1-2b2bc7dfe49c"},"task_id":"a800d573-fdf2-4d37-9bc1-2b2bc7dfe49c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a800d573-fdf2-4d37-9bc1-2b2bc7dfe49c","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree/README.md`.\n(639 line(s) above)\n640|(`AC-CLONE-005`), a second `Commit` names the terminal state, a\n641|`Prepare` past finalization is refused, and a pre-commit `Rollback`\n642|forgets the operation so a fresh `Prepare` restages the recovery\n643|retry. Every armed point is\n644|consumption-checked, so an arm the drive never reaches fails its\n645|test; all five points are driven through the `Transactor`, including\n646|rollback-enter. Eight `Fuzz*` targets drive the argv, member-path, env-name,\n647|redact, escape, render, guard-resolve, and case-collision entries\n648|through one shared `Driver` that seed-corpus tests prove reaches\n649|production (22 arrivals per entry); the env-name and redact targets\n650|additionally pin the poles a no-op gate fails (refused empty /\n651|admitted well-formed name; rewritten secret / passing innocuous\n652|line). Every target is registered in the configured validation\n653|matrix. The hostile roster derives 18 classes from the pinned\n654|specification text (every quote verified in its section) with members\n655|generated from Unicode tables and `scalar` predicates rather than the\n656|gates under test; every roster `Gate` is pinned and driven through\n657|the production entry it names, the bidi vocabulary is pinned\n658|rune-for-rune with corpus coverage, plus a symlink-escape commit\n659|witness gated on a probed capability. Capability probes (`symlink`,\n660|`fifo`, `mode-bits`, `nonroot`) each really attempt their\n661|capability — symlink create+Lstat, `mkfifo`+Lstat, `chmod 000`\n662|denial, uid check — and each gates a named test (symlink-escape\n663|commit witness, fifo byte-exchange fixture, mode-bits/nonroot denial\n664|test); they skip only where the platform cannot provide and fail on\n665|strict platforms where absence is unexpected (symlink and fifo are\n666|strict on linux and darwin, pinned exactly). `Require` takes a minimal\n667|testing handle so both the skip and the fail arms are driven through\n668|the real function with a recording fake; `TestMain` prints the\n669|process-wide report after every test, including the parallel ones.\n670|The per-test skip\n671|datum is the `--- SKIP` lines under `go test -v` (0 on darwin/arm64\n672|non-root); the final report line witnesses the counters after the\n673|whole suite, which honestly reads zero where every probe passes.\n674|\n675|Run the focused tests, race, coverage, and fuzz smoke with:\n676|\n677|```bash\n678|go test ./internal/secconftest -count=1\n679|go test ./internal/secconftest -race -count=1\n(more lines below)"}}}
