{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c94f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b60-5dda-7951-9c64-98cc389b396d"},"sequence":770,"recorded_at":1780531400001535,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"2b5b1e30-ed41-4168-ab5b-a03a807c76eb"},"task_id":"2b5b1e30-ed41-4168-ab5b-a03a807c76eb","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"2b5b1e30-ed41-4168-ab5b-a03a807c76eb","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree/README.md`.\n(954 line(s) above)\n955|previously carried whole member sets outside the inventory. The scanned file set\n956|is derived from the package directory rather than a hand-written list, and every\n957|inventoried validator must be reachable from an exported entry point. The one\n958|production call whose member slice is computed rather than literal is the\n959|Session Event payload gate; its members are pinned separately against\n960|`testdata/session-event-payload-members.md`, mechanically extracted from the\n961|pinned specification's `Exact payload members` tables, and any other computed\n962|call site fails until it is declared and given its own pin. The Session Record provenance\n963|fixture inventory also derives every required nested-object path and proves that\n964|both `null` and scalar substitutions are refused by both identity entries.\n965|Manifest entry destination-case\n966|collision detection uses a linear Unicode simple-fold set; a production-entry\n967|regression covers the declared 65,536-entry maximum inside the encoded identity\n968|size cap. Entry-local path OVERLAP is refused by the same scan: an entry whose\n969|ancestor is a declared `file`, `symlink` or `hardlink` is rejected, reusing the\n970|strict bytewise order the scan already proves rather than re-deriving each\n971|path's ancestor set, so a symlink or file parent cannot carry children into\n972|materialization.\n973|The shared strict decoder behind `Canonicalize` and both identity entries\n974|enforces a declared 256-container nesting bound: a document that opens a 257th\n975|nested object or array is refused with the typed `ErrInvalidJSON` error before\n976|any recursion can exhaust the goroutine stack, which Go otherwise reports as an\n977|uncatchable fatal runtime error. The bound leaves more than sixfold headroom\n978|over the deepest normative closed shape (the 16-level submodule tree) and stays\n979|far below encoding/json's 10,000-level cap, so it is always the first gate a\n980|deep peer object meets. The suite pins the literal value, proves accept-at-limit\n981|and refuse-past-limit at every public entry in array, object, and mixed\n982|container shapes, and replays the original 2,000,000-byte nested-array crash\n983|input as a typed refusal.\n984|The AX safe-integer refusal is not part of `Canonicalize` and must not be: RFC\n(more lines below)"}}}
