kers {\\n\\t\\t\\tif wordMatches(marker, lowered) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tmarks = append(marks, marker)\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tfm, _ := CheckAdvertisements(m.text, states)\\n\\t\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"line %d admitted=%v neg=%v markers=%v text=%.60s\\\\n\\\", m.line, len(fm) == 0, neg, marks, m.text)\\n\\t\\tif len(fm) == 0 && !neg && len(marks) == 1 {\\n\\t\\t\\tcover[marks[0]]++\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tfor _, marker := range nonClaimMarkers {\\n\\t\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"marker %-10q sole-classifies %d\\\\n\\\", marker, cover[marker])\\n\\t}\\n}\\nEOF\\ngo test ./internal/cigate/ -run TestZZProbeNotes -v -count=1 2>&1 | head -n 60; rm internal/cigate/zz_probe_test.go\",\n  \"description\": \"Probe mention arms with production matchers\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"=== RUN   TestZZProbeNotes\\nMENTIONS: 22\\nall-unavailable findings: 0\\nline 659 admitted=true neg=true markers=[probes capability attempt gates test witness skip strict platform lstat mkfifo chmod uid pinned fixture denial fail check] text=Capability probes (`symlink`, `fifo`, `mode-bits`, `nonroot`\\nline 738 admitted=true neg=false markers=[probes] text=- The `fifo` probes exchange bytes through a real kernel pip\\nline 738 admitted=true neg=false markers=[skip] text=- The `fifo` lane takes the skip path where the kernel withh\\nline 739 admitted=true neg=false markers=[witness] text=- The `fifo` byte exchange ends with a commit witness.\\nline 740 admitted=true neg=false markers=[mkfifo] text=- The `fifo` probe builds its channel with mkfifo.\\nline 741 admitted=true neg=false markers=[fixture] text=- That `fifo` exchange is the byte-exchange fixture.\\nline 742 admitted=true neg=false markers=[capability] text=- Each `symlink` capability entry names one escape probe.\\nline 743 admitted=true neg=false markers=[attempt] text=- Every `symlink` attempt runs against a guarded directory.\\nline 744 admitted=true neg=false markers=[gates] text=- The `symlink` gates admit creation inside the root.\\nline 745 admitted=true neg=false markers=[test] text=- The `symlink` test commits through the escape lane.\\nline 746 admitted=true neg=false markers=[strict] text=- Both `symlink` lanes stay strict on linux and darwin.\\nline 747 admitted=true neg=false markers=[platform] text=- The `mode-bits` verdict differs per platform.\\nline 748 admitted=true neg=false markers=[chmod] text=- The `mode-bits` lane drives chmod 000.\\nline 749 admitted=true neg=false markers=[uid] text=- The `mode-bits` lane records the acting uid.\\nline 750 admitted=true neg=false markers=[pinned] text=- The `mode-bits` expectation is pinned exactly.\\nline 751 admitted=true neg=false markers=[rejected] text=- An unexpected `mode-bits` layout is rejected.\\nline 752 admitted=true neg=false markers=[lstat] text=- The `nonroot` refusal cites lstat output.\\nline 753 admitted=true neg=false markers=[denial] text=- The `nonroot` denial names the member.\\nline 754 admitted=true neg=false markers=[fail] text=- A `nonroot` violation ends in fail.\\nline 755 admitted=true neg=false markers=[check] text=- The `nonroot` check compares identities in memory.\\nline 756 admitted=true neg=false markers=[scan] text=- The `nonroot` scan walks the live counters.\\nline 993 admitted=true neg=true markers=[strict rejected scan] text=Entry-local path OVERLAP is refused by the same scan: an ent\\nmarker \\\"probes\\\"   sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"capability\\\" sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"attempt\\\"  sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"gates\\\"    sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"test\\\"     sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"witness\\\"  sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"skip\\\"     sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"strict\\\"   sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"platform\\\" sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"lstat\\\"    sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"mkfifo\\\"   sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"chmod\\\"    sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"uid\\\"      sole-classifies 1\\nmarker \\\"pinned\\\" 