{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d39b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b60-5dda-7951-9c64-98cc389b396d"},"sequence":2088,"recorded_at":1780531400004171,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"d6b4d8ef-6209-45b9-87d6-5561c2ecd489"},"task_id":"d6b4d8ef-6209-45b9-87d6-5561c2ecd489","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"d6b4d8ef-6209-45b9-87d6-5561c2ecd489","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree/LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-07\n7|\n8|### 33xcnc round 2: review F1/F2/F3 closed test-only, 70/71 battery on the corrected 101-exit denominator\n9|- SCOPE (test-only; no production touched, frozen files intact): `internal/environ/shape_census_test.go` (load-bearing delegation pins + 9 synthetic decoy controls), `tuple_agreement_test.go` (uppercase-hex fingerprint vector), `frame_agreement_test.go` (per-member duplicate sweeper over 30 production-derived keys × 4 judges), `decode_unit_test.go` (R_digestnonstr downstream pin), `internal/provhost/protocol_test.go` (DecodeResponse per-member duplicate test, 6 derived + 4 foreign keys).\n10|- F1 (decoy defeated the gate): `pinsCheckDelegation`/`pinsDelegation` required only an `environ` reference, so `_, _ = environ.CheckDigest(raw)` + a regrown `ParseDigest(ToLower)` copy stayed green while `sessadapter.DecodeTuple` admitted uppercase-hex fingerprints `environ` refuses. Fix: helpers must be exactly `return environ.Twin(args)` with twin-name match; wrappers must attribute the owner verdict to reused non-blank names with no other call, plus a duplicate-rule check. The plant now fails `TestCheckHelpersDelegateToEnviron` AND `TestTupleAgreementAcrossFacades/uppercase_fingerprint_refused`; harness mutants D1/D2 report `suites=behavioral,census`.\n11|- F2 (duplicate class measured at one key): narrowing `duplicate && key != K` survived 6/8 response keys and 7/10 owner keys. Fix: derivation-backed sweepers (member sets derived from tuple/observation/response/scan-request production; new members auto-swept) through `DecodeTuple`/`CheckScanRequest`/`DecodeManifest`/`DecodeResponse`/`DecodeStrictObject`. Battery adds 8 owner + 6 retained narrowing mutants, one per survived key. Survivor honest-report: first `P_dupnarrow_provider_id` run SURVIVED and exposed a real test gap (foreign `provider_id` missing from the envelope sweeper); key added, mutant re-run KILLED.\n12|- F3 (denominator basis): corrected — 31 refuse sites + 59 bool-false + 11 `&Fault{}` frame exits = 101 (105 counting the 4 bool-`return <expr>` arms: CheckEnvironmentID/CheckSemver/isNull/rawUint53-forward). The \"27 of 100\" figure was the corrected basis pre-ladder-guard; 90 was the uncorrected one. Harness derives all three components at runtime; F3 residue exits attacked by N1/M15/M15n/M16/M17/M17n inside the previously excluded 11.\n13|- EVIDENCE: battery `/tmp/mutbattery_leaf6/run.py` + `battery.log` + `results.json`: 70 killed / 71 applied (49 narrowing incl. D1 token-preserving delegation decoy + 8 owner + 6 retained duplicate narrowings; 17 arm-deletion incl. D2; 3 census-only; 1 audit-only; H1 NOT_APPLIED + H2 COMPILE_FAIL distinct rows; 1 predicted survivor R_digestnonstr, now property-pinned by `TestDigestBridgeRefusesEmptyDownstream`). Mutant table + outcome attached as round-2 resources.\n14|- GATES: `go build` + `go vet` + `GOOS=windows` build/vet exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok), `go test ./... -race` exit 0 (23 ok, full repo — no race bound this round), `-cover` (env 92.4/sess 82.0/dir 87.7/ph 86.0/scalar 90.1/invcore 70.2).\n15|- STATUS: handed off to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\n16|\n17|### 1215 — 33xcnc: remaining environment copies converged, residue re-derived, 54/55 battery\n18|- SCOPE: TASK-260906-33xcnc (story final leaf). Production: `sessadapter/decode.go` + `dirnode/decode.go` (9 Check*/measure/extensions helpers each delegate to `environ.*`, 6 grammar vars deleted, rawUint53 trailing arm + ladder empty-guard hardened to the environ texture), grammar call sites (`sessadapter/manifest.go`, `tuple.go`, `probe.go`, `dirnode/probe.go`, `query.go`), `provhost/opdecode.go` (same trailing arm), `environ/decode.go` (ladder guard, refuse func→var). No leaf-owned production touched (`provhost/protocol.go`, `identity.go`, `probe.go`, `canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go` frozen). Tests: scalar agreement battery (15 vectors), site audit (31 sites/39 rules, TestMain swap + recorder), census alias audit (import-alias/var-binding/dot-import/shadow plants), delegation pins, sibling trailing units, ladder/array units.\n19|- FINDING (ladder hole, caught by the new unit pre-fix): `parseUint53Literal(\"\")` admitted 0 in all three packages; unreachable via rawUint53 (guarded) but hardened identically everywhere.\n20|- FINDING (union coverage): in-package + external test files compile to one binary, so the TestMain audit sees exercised sites from both; the in-package driver table is load-bearing for the two frame-fault passthrough sites (external corpora carry no frame-faulty tuple/observation bodies). Proven: dropping one passthrough driver fails the closed rule set (`want exactly 39 codes, observed 38`).\n21|- FINDING (mutant quality): M13n v1 (presence skip without decode skip) survived — the nil member refuses at decode fall-through. v2 (with `continue`) kills. R_rawstringerr predicted-survivor was wrong: direct-rawString arms (platform/arch/version/provider) refuse at the wrong arm, killed by exact-text drivers.\n22|- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-33xcnc_outcome.md` + battery log + mutants JSON + harness + mutant table (54 killed/55 applied on denominator 90 = 31 refuse + 59 bool; 34 narrowing incl. T1/C3 token-preserving raw-scans; 3 census-only; 1 audit-only; 1 predicted survivor R_digestnonstr with downstream-hold bound; H1/H2 prove NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL rows). Callerless closed for 10 Check* symbols via delegation; DecodeTuple/DecodeEnvironmentObservation/rawUint53/Fault.Error/HasLoneSurrogateEscape re-stated with reasons.\n23|- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok), `-race` exit 0 (environ/sessadapter/dirnode/scalar/provhost/canonicaljson/provider; full-repo race not run), `-cover` exit 0 (env 92.4/sess 82.0/dir 87.7/ph 86.0/scalar 90.1), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` + both builds exit 0, gofmt clean, tracecheck exit 0, catalog current, cigate selections exit 0, fuzz smoke 13/13.\n24|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review. Open need (in outcome, no board element): provhost decoder convergence needs unfreezing `provhost/protocol.go`.\n25|\n26|### 1111 — 2okwyf round 4: F3 stray file out of the tree, N1/N2 instrument gates fail closed, N3/N4 bounds\n27|- SCOPE: TASK-260906-2okwyf rework (review rev3 CHANGES REQUESTED, blocking F3 + non-blocking N1–N4). F3: `probe_f2_main.go.bak` (F2 probe, `package main`, repo root) moved to `.temp/TASK-260906-2okwyf/` (gitignored, outside the candidate tree; `git status` clean of it). No production behavior change this round. Test instrument only: `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (refusalArm gains the derivation-time `backendID` AST-key flag; `deriveRefusalArmsIn` dir parameter), `backend_id_entry_census_test.go` (site filter reads the flag — any composite-literal spelling; entry enumeration fails closed on bare-name collision via `collectExportedEntries`; two synthetic-package-dir derivation tests; N3 stated bound for the 44 free-entry reasons). LOGBOOK: N4 number/typo fixes (59 derived = 10 pair + 5 hostile-only + 44 free; round-2 entry cited rev1, not rev3).\n28|- FINDING (holes reproduced pre-fix, both GREEN on the old tree): P2 exported method `(*Registry).Reconcile` absorbed by the bare-name dedupe; P3 dead multi-line BackendID arm missed by the line-text filter. Post-fix both RED in one `TestBackendIDEntryCensus` run: `has no census pair` for the multiline site, `collide on one bare name: Reconcile: Reconcile in manifest.go against Registry.Reconcile in manifest.go`. Plants reverted byte-identical (`git diff` shows no PLANT; full suite green).\n29|- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-2okwyf_outcome-r4.md` + `TASK-260906-2okwyf_battery-r4.json` + `TASK-260906-2okwyf_mutants-r4.json` (r4: 5 applied — narrowing 2, arm-deletion 2, census-only 1 — 4 killed / 1 survived with a plant-evidenced bound; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct controls; masks non-empty: census 15, behav 32). Continuity re-runs on this tree: r1 9/9, r2 5/5, r3 6/6 killed, 0 survived — cumulative 24/25 with the single survivor D-tb-entryindex-enforce (0 live collisions; P2 plant GREEN without the gate, RED with it). N3 deliberately left open with the 0-of-44 sweep bound. Candidate tree OID in the outcome doc, detached-index write-tree AFTER this append, `ls-tree` read back against the scope enumeration both directions.\n30|- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok, 0 FAIL), `-race` terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (tb 95.4%, ph 86.0%, pv 97.8%), `go vet ./...` exit 0, `GOOS=windows go vet` (tb/ph/pv) exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean.\n(more lines below)"}}}
