{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d3e3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07b60-5dda-7951-9c64-98cc389b396d"},"sequence":2124,"recorded_at":1780531400004243,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bd52028a-acb2-4196-94e2-c06d1bbe961a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"abb39906-01aa-4b62-a265-efd701930da4"},"task_id":"abb39906-01aa-4b62-a265-efd701930da4","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"abb39906-01aa-4b62-a265-efd701930da4","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-07\n-\n-### 33xcnc round 2: review F1/F2/F3 closed test-only, 70/71 battery on the corrected 101-exit denominator\n+## 2026-09-07\n+\n+### 9ny4xl: R1–R6 closed — probe-availability claims corrected, marker census measures effect, catalog directive pinned\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260907-9ny4xl (story final leaf). `internal/cigate` claim tests + effect census + splitter tests + `doc.go`, `internal/catalog` directive pin, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` comments + freshness guard, README CI table + 20 probe notes, 2249 correction below. Leaves 1–5 production untouched; `claims.go` production changed only in comments; `catalog.go` production unchanged.\n+- R1: the capability-claims comment and the 2249 entry stated `ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site; `claims.go:235` reads it into the availability map. Both now state what `doc.go` states: the gate reads `Available` from its input states (both postures driven), and what reaches no availability reader is the live probe outcome (`ProbeStates` feeds only `CapabilityIDs`, which drops availability). New `TestAvailabilityFieldDrivesVerdict` refuses/admits the same claim across postures (battery N-avail-false/true killed).\n+- R2: the derive-targets comment named the grep + size check as the fail-closed guards. Re-measured with a real empty-leg replica (`secconftest` + fuzzless `axerror`): grep refuses nothing (pipeline status discarded), `test -s` passes (8 lines), only the count pin refuses (8 vs 13, exit 1). Comment now names the pin; neighbouring steps audited (PASS-guard loops, gofmt/coverage/fixture count guards, target-match diff, elapsed grep) — no same mistake.\n+- R3: the marker census measured occurrence while markers classified 0 of 2 mentions. New `TestEveryNonClaimMarkerClassifiesCorpusSentence` asserts the resolving arm per mention from the production predicates cross-checked against the production verdict, and requires every marker to sole-classify at least one corpus sentence. 20 probe notes added to the README CI section (one sole-classifier per marker); measured distribution negation 2 / marker 20 / refused 0. README cell corrected to \"negated or marker-classified non-claim context\". Old corpus + new census fails (battery C-old-corpus); dropped-list X3 now dies (was a survivor).\n+- R4: new `TestSameBlockSentencesSplitOnTerminal` (period/bang/query rows, same-block negated+positive pair) kills the paragraph-granularity narrowing (N-split-X1) and the dot-only narrowing (N-split-dot-only).\n+- R5 (bound, re-measured this session): 13/13 smoke targets print `fuzz: elapsed`; `secconftest/FuzzRedactCorpus` + all four `canonicaljson` targets spend `-fuzztime=100x` on baseline coverage and never print `now fuzzing` (8 reach mutation). Stated in the README row and the smoke-step comment with the escape (budget/corpus change moves it silently).\n+- R6 (bound ANSWERED): the rev2 \"Linux execution unverified\" unknown is closed by the landing PR run — PR #36 (STORY-260830-1i3qu7, merged 2026-09-06) shows `Conformance fixtures (ubuntu-latest, internal/secprim)` and `(ubuntu-latest, internal/secconftest)` pass in both runs, with macOS legs and every other job green (`gh pr checks 36`, observed this session).\n+- CARRIED (pre-existing, fixed here): `//go:generate` → `// go:generate` disarmed the generator while the token survived and the freshness diff stayed clean (reproduced: old step exits 0 on the rewrite). Fix: anchored `grep -c '^//go:generate'` pin in the freshness step + committed `TestGenerateDirectiveStaysRecognizedForm`; the rewrite now fails the guard (exit 1) and the pin while catalog/cataloggen stay otherwise green (battery G-directive-space, behavioral suite executed).\n+- RECORDED (pre-existing, not fixed — traceability scope): `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` is a `bytes.Contains` gate over `ci.yml`: moving the Vet step's `run: go vet ./...` into a YAML comment keeps it green (doubly blind — `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` carries the same substring). Re-attacked this session (PASS on the blinded tree, ci.yml restored byte-identical). At HEAD before every leaf of both stories; named here beside the `go:generate` one per the rev2 verdict.\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_outcome.md` (5/5 AC rows with call sites, battery table, tree OID, exact changed paths) + `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_mutants.log` + `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_change-request.patch` on the board task. Battery 14 applied / 14 killed / 0 survivors (narrowing 10 incl. the token-preserving directive rewrite, arm-deletion 3, census-only 1; C-old-corpus census control; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct harness rows; audit-only 0 — no AST audit in this CR's scope).\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (23 ok), `-race ./...` exit 0 (23 ok, full repo), `-cover` exit 0 (cigate 90.5%, secprim 94.4%, secconftest 92.6%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (60 contracts / 98 cases, unchanged), catalog current, capability-claims + contract-preservation steps verbatim 6/6 + 6/6, fuzz smoke 13/13 elapsed (5 baseline-only, 8 mutation).\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps). Story-final CR: no board element created under STORY-260905-3t31e9; follow-up needs are listed in the outcome, not the board.\n+\n+### 33xcnc round 2: review F1/F2/F3 closed test-only, 70/71 battery on the corrected 101-exit denominator\n"}}}
